00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.599 align:start position:0%
just a few months ago the prospect of  these Thai youngsters soaking up the  atmosphere at the theater of dreams  would have been just that but today for  the wild boars their dreams became a  reality when the boys were rescued after  being trapped in a flooded cave  Manchester United told them they would  be welcome to visit and they were true  to their word  josie marino met the team at the club's  training ground yesterday and they got a  behind-the-scenes trip to Old Trafford -  today they were back again to watch the  Premier League encounter against Everton  in July the boys spent over two weeks in  the flooded cave complex near chiang rai  with no sunlight limited oxygen and  rationed food and water it took three  days to get them out with some of the  boys suffering lung infections after  their ordeal one of the divers who made  repeated trips into the cave to rescue  the team today is a proud moment we  never thought that we could get them all  out even when we first started that  first day as rescue there was always a  chance you know there was going to be a  some sort of incident and they could get  fatality but yeah I was impressed when  we finished then we actually gone  although if we get to the meeting the  mom sure it'd be quite emotional maybe  maybe maybe some tears coming out then  but I don't know this has been an  incredible few weeks for the wild boars  a remarkable story of first survival and  now almost celebrity status all of it  faced together as a team Fraser Maud Sky  News Manchester
 

